course: dictionary
lesson: 3286
title: Words from the café
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from another country or another language. Context helps you find their meaning. «In France un café is a small strong black coffee (an espresso); children usually order un chocolat chaud, un jus d'orange or une limonade.» The brackets tell you straight away: an espresso is a small strong black coffee.
explain: The list after the semicolon shows what children usually order: hot chocolate, orange juice and lemonade. Espresso is not on that list. This tells you it is a drink for grown-ups, not the sort of drink children usually choose.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «a small strong black coffee» in place of espresso, and the sentence still makes sense. That means your meaning is right.
fact: Espresso is a strong, dark coffee made by forcing very hot water through finely ground coffee beans.
fact: An espresso is one small cup of this coffee.
fact: Espresso is the base of many coffee drinks, such as cappuccino and latte.
fact: Espresso has lots of caffeine, which is not good for children.
fact: Phrases to know: «a shot of espresso», «double espresso», «espresso machine».
exercise: «In France un café is a small strong black coffee (an espresso).» What is an espresso? | A glass of orange juice | A fizzy lemonade | A sweet hot chocolate | *A small, strong, dark coffee
exercise: Which drink is NOT on the list of drinks children usually order? | Une limonade | Un jus d'orange | Un chocolat chaud | *Un espresso
exercise: Ruby reads «un café» and asks what espresso means. What is the best swap for espresso in the sentence? | A glass of juice | A sweet milky drink | A cold fizzy drink | *A small strong black coffee
test: Which phrase describes a machine that makes coffee? | Hot chocolate maker | *Espresso machine | Lemonade stand | Double orange
test: Why is espresso not a good drink for children? | It has no colour | It is too cold | It is too sweet | *It has lots of caffeine
exam: What does espresso mean? | *A strong, dark coffee made by forcing very hot water through finely ground coffee beans | A tea made with milk | A cake eaten at breakfast | A small glass of juice
